air/OS (Haiku arm64): Mesa 26.2.4's PowerVR Vulkan driver on the native
"powervr" kernel driver (/dev/graphics/powervr/0, Cubie A7S BXM-4-64 MC1).

The kernel takes Linux's drm.h / pvr_drm.h structures unchanged behind op
codes PVR_HAIKU_OP(nr) (headers/private/graphics/powervr/pvr_haiku.h in the
air/OS tree, put on the include path by build.sh, not copied). All changes are
#ifdef __HAIKU__ or Haiku-only meson except two in pvr_physical_device.c, a
NULL check and an assert fix; a Linux build of this tree is otherwise
unchanged (build.sh builds the host tools and the drm-shim smoke test from
it).

  include/drm-uapi/drm.h            BSD ioctl encoding from <bsd/sys/ioccom.h>
  include/drm-uapi/pvr_drm.h        no <linux/const.h>, <linux/types.h>: _BITULL
