  pvr_rt_dataset.[ch], pvr_device.h, a device cache of idle render target data
  pvr_arch_device.c,                sets (HWRT data set + local free list) for
  pvr_arch_cmd_buffer.c             dynamic rendering. Every
                                    vkCmdBeginRendering() (zink's every render
                                    pass) has its own render state, and so
                                    created both and destroyed them when the
                                    command buffer was reset: firmware objects,
                                    buffers, VM maps and synchronous firmware
                                    cleanups in the kernel, every frame. A data
                                    set still belongs to one render state at a
                                    time; once that is cleaned up (its command
                                    buffer no longer pending) the next
                                    rendering of the same width, height,
                                    samples and layers takes it. At most 16
                                    idle ones are kept, and one is destroyed
                                    after 256 later releases (old sizes age
